        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "***3 BED FAMILY HOME / EXCELLENT TRANQUIL LOCATION / LARGE GARDEN***\r\n\r\nKELLY BRADSHAW are delighted to present to the market 13 Belton Park Gardens, Donnycarney, Dublin 9, an opportunity to acquire a family home.\r\n\r\nThis is a three-bedroom mid terrace family home located in a quiet cul de sac off Collins Avenue.\r\n\r\nOn entering this property, there is a well-proportioned hallway with understairs storage and a downstairs WC. To the right is a bright spacious living room with an original feature fireplace. Next is the dining/kitchen area which is bright and spacious with a fireplace and gas fire. From the kitchen, the back door leads out to a north facing generous sized back garden. There is also a large shed in the garden. This shed backs onto the closed private laneway which residents have a key for.\r\n\r\nUpstairs the spacious landing area opens to 3 bedrooms, one of which has an original fireplace. There is a fully tiled bathroom with a large accessible shower on this floor.   Up again is a converted attic for storage use.\r\n\r\n13 Belton Park Gardens will prove popular with first time buyers and families alike. All necessary amenities on your doorstep. The location of this home is both quiet and yet highly convenient. The property is superbly situated only a stone's throw from amenities such as shops, restaurants, and public transport links providing easy access to the City Centre. It is located in the community of Donnycarney parish.  \r\n\r\nWithin convenient reach is Beaumont Hospital. There are a number of well established local Primary and Secondary schools in the Donnycarney, Marino and Artane areas. Further amenities in the locality include Dublin City University, Maryfield College Secondary School, Dominican College and Ard Scoil Rs. Croke Park, Westwood Gym, Regency Leisure Centre, Clontarf Golf Club, Whitehall Colmcille and St Vincent's GAA are all only a short distance away. There are also a number of efficient bus routes on your doorstep including the 27, 14 and 15 which brings you to Clontarf and Killester Dart station.\r\n\r\nThe property is in need of refurbishment and some modernisation.\r\n\r\nEarly viewing comes highly recommended."
      },
